==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|perturben}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|perturber}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|perturbare||throw into confusion, confuse, disorder, disturb}}, from {{m|la|per||through}} + {{m|la|turbare||to confuse, disturb}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/pɚˈtɝb/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-perturb.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(r)b|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[disturb]]; to bother or unsettle.
# {{lb|en|physics}} To slightly modify the motion of an object.
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} To modify the motion of a body by exerting a gravitational force.
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} To modify slightly, such as an equation or value.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|perturbation}}
* {{l|en|perturbative}}
* {{l|en|perturbed}}
* {{l|en|perturbedly}}

